          "en": "\"Whenever I went out among the people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had left, it grieved me to see no one but a man [suspected](g:maghmus) of hypocrisy, or one of the weak whom Allah had excused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not mention me until he reached Tabuk. Sitting among the people at Tabuk, he said: What has Ka'b done? A man of Banu Salimah said: Messenger of Allah, his two cloaks and his [admiring glances at himself](g:itf) have kept him back. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: What an evil thing to say! By Allah, Messenger of Allah, we know nothing of him but good. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was silent.\""
